{"title":"Career Roadmap · Parametric Designer","role":"Parametric Designer","summary":"A Parametric Designer uses computational methods to create, modify, analyze and optimize complex design systems. Instead of manually producing every design variation, the designer creates rules, relationships and algorithms that generate multiple design solutions.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Arch (Bachelor of Architecture)","Course":"Digital Architecture / Computational Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"A Parametric Designer uses computational methods to create, modify, analyze and optimize complex design systems. Instead of manually producing every design variation, the designer creates rules, relationships and algorithms that generate multiple design solutions."},{"type":"p","text":"For a B.Arch graduate, this career combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"Computational geometry"},{"text":"Parametric modelling"},{"text":"Algorithmic design"},{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"Geometry processing"},{"text":"Environmental analysis"},{"text":"Digital fabrication"},{"text":"Optimization"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The core mindset is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Traditional Design","Draw Geometry","Modify Geometry Manually"]},{"type":"flow","items":["Parametric Design","Define Rules + Relationships","Generate Geometry","Change Parameters","Generate New Variations","Evaluate + Optimize"]},{"type":"p","text":"A Parametric Designer can work in architecture, façade design, structural geometry, urban design, computational fabrication, product design, building performance and digital construction."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizon","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Stage","Primary Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Year 1"},{"text":"Architecture + computational thinking"}],[{"text":"Year 2"},{"text":"3D modelling + Grasshopper fundamentals"}],[{"text":"Year 3"},{"text":"Advanced parametric modelling + scripting"}],[{"text":"Year 4"},{"text":"Computational design + fabrication + optimization"}],[{"text":"0–2 years"},{"text":"Junior Computational / Parametric Designer"}],[{"text":"2–5 years"},{"text":"Parametric Designer / Computational Designer"}],[{"text":"5–8 years"},{"text":"Senior Computational Designer"}],[{"text":"8+ years"},{"text":"Computational Design Lead / Digital Design Specialist"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-Wise Roadmap","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Architecture + Computational Thinking"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong architectural fundamentals first."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Architectural design"},{"text":"Geometry"},{"text":"Design principles"},{"text":"Architectural representation"},{"text":"Basic mathematics"},{"text":"Perspective"},{"text":"2D/3D visualization"},{"text":"Building systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Software"},{"type":"p","text":"Start with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AutoCAD"},{"text":"SketchUp"},{"text":"Rhino basics"},{"text":"Revit basics"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Computational thinking"},{"type":"p","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Variables"},{"text":"Parameters"},{"text":"Relationships"},{"text":"Functions"},{"text":"Coordinates"},{"text":"Transformations"},{"text":"Conditions"},{"text":"Iteration"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Example:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Building Width = W"},{"text":"Building Height = H"},{"text":"Window Ratio = R"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Change W","Geometry changes","Window positions change","Façade changes"]}]},{"heading":"Year 2 — Rhino + Grasshopper","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"This is the critical foundation for the career."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn Rhino"},{"type":"p","text":"Master:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Curves"},{"text":"Surfaces"},{"text":"Solids"},{"text":"NURBS"},{"text":"SubD basics"},{"text":"Boolean operations"},{"text":"Layers"},