e constraints"},{"text":"Program"},{"text":"Environmental requirements"},{"text":"Cost"},{"text":"Structural constraints"},{"text":"The designer's role becomes increasingly focused on setting objectives, constraints and evaluation criteria."}]},{"type":"h","text":"2. Generative Engineering"},{"type":"p","text":"Instead of designing one solution:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Constraints","Algorithm","100s / 1000s of Options","Performance Evaluation","Optimization","Selected Design"]},{"type":"h","text":"3. Digital Twins"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parametric models can connect with operational building data."},{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Parametric Model"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"IoT"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Building Data","Digital Twin"]},{"type":"h","text":"4. Robotic Construction"},{"type":"p","text":"Computational geometry can directly control robotic processes for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Robotic milling"},{"text":"Robotic assembly"},{"text":"Automated fabrication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"5. AI-Assisted Coding"},{"type":"p","text":"AI coding tools can help designers create:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Grasshopper scripts"},{"text":"Python automation"},{"text":"Revit workflows"},{"text":"Custom computational tools"},{"text":"But the designer still needs to understand geometry, algorithms and design logic to validate the output."}]},{"type":"h","text":"6. Real-Time Environmental Optimization"},{"type":"p","text":"Future workflows increasingly connect:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parametric Model"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Climate Data"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Simulation"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Optimization","High-Performance Design"]}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Minimum employability stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Arch"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Grasshopper"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Parametric Modelling"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Architectural Design"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Basic Python"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Geometry"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"1–2 Advanced Parametric Projects"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Portfolio"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Relevant Internship"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Strong candidate stack"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"B.Arch"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Grasshopper"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Advanced Data Trees"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Python"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"C#"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Revit"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Dynamo"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Ladybug / Honeybee"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Digital Fabrication"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"BIM Automation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Environmental Simulation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Real-World Computational Project"}]}]},{"heading":"Target Profile by Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"By graduation, the student should be capable of taking a design problem and turning it into a parameterized computational system."},{"type":"flow","items":["Design Problem","Identify Variables","Define Relationships","Build Grasshopper Algorithm","Generate Alternatives","Analyse Performance","Optimize","Select Design","BIM / Documentation","Fabrication / Construction"]},{"type":"h","text":"Portfolio target"},{"type":"p","text":"Build 5–6 technically strong projects:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Parametric façade"},{"text":"Parametric pavilion"},{"text":"Generative housing/layout system"},{"text":"Environmental optimization project"},{"text":"Parametric urban design"},{"text":"Digital fabrication project"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For every project, show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design problem"},{"text":"Parameters"},{"text":"Grasshopper definition"},{"text":"Algorithm logic"},{"text":"Generated alternatives"},{"text":"Evaluation criteria"},{"text":"Final solution"},{"text":"Technical drawings"},{"text":"Physical/digital prototype"}]},{"type":"p","text":"Avoid portfolios consisting only of attractive computational forms. Employers want to see why the algorithm exists and what problem it solves."}]},{"heading":"Best Overall Positioning","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"The strongest professional identity is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Architect","Computational Designer","Design Technologist"],"sep":"+"},{"type":"p","text":"rather than simply:"},{"type":"h","text":"Architect who knows Grasshopper"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"The real differentiator is the ability to combine architectural reasoning, algorithms, geometry, simulation and automation."},{"text":"Architecture"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Computational Thinking"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Parametric Modelling"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Programming"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"BIM"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Simulation"},{"text":"+"},{"text":"Optimization"},{"text":"+"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["Digital Fabrication","Computational / Parametric Design Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"This provides a strong pathway toward Parametric Designer → Computational Designer → Senior Computational Designer → Computational Design Lead / Design Technology Specialist, with adjacent opportunities in BIM automation, façade design, building performance, generative design, digital fabrication and computational architecture research."}]}]}